Day 034 - Optional Chaining

What I practiced

Using optional chaining (?.) to safely access properties that might not exist.

What I learned

* Optional chaining uses ?..
* It prevents an error when a property or object is null or undefined.
* If something before ?. is null or undefined, JavaScript returns undefined.
* It is useful when working with objects and data that may be missing.

Example

const user = {
    name: "Prashik"
};
console.log(user.name);
console.log(user.address?.city);

address does not exist, but optional chaining prevents an error.

Expected output

Prashik
undefined

Run

node day-034/script.js
